# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Node and the client's build output
node_modules/
dist/

# The certificate the server issues in the house — the private half never belongs in git
.office-mumble/

# The installers office.cmd / office.sh leave to be handed out — built for one house, never for the repository
handout/

# Certificates the harness fetched from somebody else's server
harness/.certs/

# What the harness builds: served straight from disk, never committed
harness/dist/

# A local stand's lockfile belongs to the stand, not to the repo
spike/*/Cargo.lock

# rustc will dump stack traces when hitting an internal compiler error to PWD
rustc-ice-*.txt

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# macOS writes these wherever a folder is opened
.DS_Store
._*

# What Tauri generates from the shell's configuration on every build.
client/src-tauri/gen/

# The demo recording belongs to the repository: a clone on a machine that never had it must still be able to
# start a figure that speaks. It is one fixed clip in the test voice folder, not the office's own voices —
# those never leave the machine that recorded them.

# What the server writes back: a run's plan, not a source file
fixtures/*.plan.json
